/-!
# The witnesses for `k = 6, 7, 8`

Theorem 4 of the paper for `k = 6, 7, 8`: for each witness of Appendix A, the triangle defect
`N`, the fact that no gauge costs less than `D`, and the fact that the identity gauge attains `D`.

The gauge minimum is checked by the table search of `TableSearch`. Each witness gets a table of
moved counts (`tableW6`, `tableW7`, `tableW8`), checked against the cochain by the kernel
(`tableSpec_w6`, …), and the kernel then runs the search from the identity on vertex `0`. The
`k = 8` search is split by the gauge on vertex `1` into six kernel-checked pieces.

The upstream repository checks the same three statements with the branch-and-bound search of
`Basic`, split into 309 generated pieces; the Lean Pool port replaced those pieces with this
cheaper certificate.
-/

@[expose] public section

